    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/6/66360.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, the best outcome is removal. And we've presented the vice president would own ultimatum, either you invoke the 25th Amendment or else we have no choice but to move forward with impeachment. It is clear that the vice president refuses to invoke the 25th Amendment in conjunction with a majority of the cabinet. So we have no choice but to impeach Donald Trump. The violent mob he unleashed on the US Capitol represents an unprecedented assault on the separation of powers between the Congress and the president. It represents an unprecedented assault on the peaceful transfer of power from one president to the next. If striking at the core of our constitutional republic is not an impeachable offense, then what is impeachment for?",
